{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/916339-vascu-aztecs-and-mirrors","id":916339,"title":"VASCU, Aztecs and Mirrors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T11:26:55-07:00","id":916339,"title":"VASCU, Aztecs and Mirrors","content":"so- I don't know when, how or why the God-Machine/VASCU connection was established, or how popular that theory truly is, but here something I've noticed while making my &quot;VASCU research&quot; for its Civil War- the one, weirdest, unexplained mystery VASCU has (and many would day, the only one) is the Hall of Mirrors- that future seeing Endowment which is claimed to be a &quot;shared hallucination&quot; yet still seem to describe the exact same place for all agents (including seeing each other in the Hall). Now, at Beneath the Skin (the Aztec Dark Era), there is that God Machine cult call &quot;of Huitzilopotchli the Many Wheeled&quot;, who are extremely obsessed with the calendar and the cycles of the world, recognizing their Sun God with the endless moving Machine. As one could expect, one of their benefits if Omen Sensitivity- but their 5 dot Mystery Cult benefit is the most interesting one: the ability to wrap yourself in space and go into a &quot;bolthole inside spatial dimensions&quot;, through which you can see the world as though (and I quote) a &quot;hall of mirrors&quot;. Sure, that trick is made for protection and not future divination, but still I find the connection as.. interesting.<br /> <br /> So- if there is a connection between that ancient, Aztec Cult and VASCU? Are those two &quot;halls of mirrors&quot; are one and the same, or simply a remarkably similar phenomena? Did the God Machine created the hall, or does it simply use/d it for its needs like it does with everything else? Are VASCU doing the same thing- exploiting a 