"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T09:10:50-07:00","id":916861,"title":"","content":"Note that VASCU is one of the few groups to focus on capturing/arresting the monsters rather than just shooting them, and that Aztec warriors focused on taking their opponents in alive for sacrifice...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T09:22:01-07:00","id":916867,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> In fact, it ties in with this Mystery Cult I'm writing, Modern Nahualtin.<br /> <br /> (the idea is that the secret police priests actually integrated with the conquistadores so well, that their beliefs of traditional Aztec religion merged with Catholic Christianity-they believe YHVH and Omoeteotl are one and the same. They're best described as henotheists who believe only the Guy/Gal In Charge deserves faith without expectation of recompense-all other gods are effectively angels who exist to carry out Zir will and maintain the world-and have since reinterpreted Sacrifice metaphorically; God wants you to give up part of your life in good works...and maintaining the social order. They've become a cult of shapeshifting vigilantes, enforcing societal rules through their skintheiving; making it so that they're the quiet backers of VASCU gives them an effect on the world).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T10:29:15-07:00","id":916893,"title":"","content":"Also- <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirrors_in_Mesoamerican_culture\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> must be relevant<br /> <br /> And of course, you can't talk about Aztec mirrors without mentioning Tezcatlipoca- with everything it may imply on VASCU (sure, there are technically 4 &quot;Tezcatlipocas&quot;, but if you have the option to go with the scariest one than why not?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:22:16-07:00","id":917099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/916339-vascu-aztecs-and-mirrors?p=916893#post916893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also- <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirrors_in_Mesoamerican_culture\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> must be relevant<br /> <br /> And of course, you can't talk about Aztec mirrors without mentioning Tezcatlipoca- with everything it may imply on VASCU (sure, there are technically 4 &quot;Tezcatlipocas&quot;, but if you have the option to go with the scariest one than why not?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, Black Tezcaltipoca is probably the second-most likely of his fellows to back psychic-using units the FBI (the most likely being Quetzalcoatl, of course). He's the god of Sorcery <i>and Rulership, </i>after all. &quot;Oh, these mortals wish to invoke me to better serve as the hands of their ruling government? What's the catch?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}